      "math_academy_id": "q-35299",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Determine the dimension of\n$\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{10}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, the dimension of the span is $3.$",
